title: Guard
---
// Conversations with the people of the starting town. Each NPC's `dialogue`
// (in npcs/starting_town.ron) names the node its conversation starts at.
Guard Aldren: Halt! Oh, a new face. Welcome to town, {player_name()}.
-> Any advice for a traveller?
    Guard Aldren: Stay on the roads after dark. Wolves don't.
    Guard Aldren: And the river's safe to wade where it's shallow. Mind the deep pools.
    <<jump GuardMore>>
-> What's that smoke to the south?
    Guard Aldren: That's the volcano. Don't go poking at it.
    <<jump GuardMore>>
-> Goodbye.
    Guard Aldren: Keep your wits about you.
===

title: GuardMore
---
Guard Aldren: Anything else?
-> What's there to do around here?
    Guard Aldren: Hilda at the forge could use a hand, and Elsie always needs flour carried.
    Guard Aldren: Old Tomas knows every story in these hills, if you've an afternoon to spare.
-> That's all, thanks.
    Guard Aldren: Safe travels, {player_name()}.
===

title: Smith
---
Hilda: Welcome to my forge, {player_name()}!
Hilda: The fire isn't lit yet, I'm afraid. Come back soon and I'll have blades to sell.
-> Have you seen Old Tomas's pipe? <<if quest_stage("tomas_pipe") == "asked">>
    <<if has_room_for("old_pipe")>>
        Hilda: A pipe? There was one by the anvil this morning. Reeks of cherry tobacco.
        Hilda: That'll be his, all right. Here, take it to him.
        <<give_item old_pipe>>
        <<set_quest tomas_pipe found>>
    <<else>>
        Hilda: I've got it here, but your hands are full. Make some room in your inventory and come back.
    <<endif>>
-> What will you make?
    Hilda: Swords, axes, pickaxes. Whatever a body needs to make their way out there.
    Hilda: Bring me ore and I'll teach you to work it yourself.
-> I'll come back later.
    Hilda: Mind the anvil on your way out.
===

title: Tomas
---
<<if quest_stage("tomas_pipe") == "done">>
    Old Tomas: Ah, {player_name()}! Still puffing away on my old pipe, thanks to you.
<<elseif item_count("old_pipe") > 0>>
    Old Tomas: Is that... my pipe? You found it!
    <<take_item old_pipe>>
    <<set_quest tomas_pipe done>>
    <<give_miasma 30>>
    Old Tomas: Here, take this for your trouble. And a story, whenever you like.
<<elseif quest_stage("tomas_pipe") == "asked">>
    Old Tomas: Any sign of my pipe? I'm sure I had it at the forge.
<<else>>
    Old Tomas: Eh? Oh, hello there, young {player_name()}.
<<endif>>
-> Tell me a story.
    <<jump TomasStory>>
-> Have you lost something? <<if quest_stage("tomas_pipe") == "">>
    Old Tomas: My pipe! I had it this morning. Or was that yesterday?
    Old Tomas: I was at the forge, chatting with Hilda. If you find it, I'd be ever so grateful.
    <<set_quest tomas_pipe asked>>
-> Goodbye, Tomas.
    Old Tomas: Mind how you go.
===

title: TomasStory
---
Old Tomas: When I was your age, these hills were all forest.
Old Tomas: They say the dwarves dig so deep they hear the world's heart beating.
-> Another one!
    Old Tomas: Elsie's bread is the best in three valleys. Don't tell her I said so.
    Old Tomas: That's not a story, you say? Well, it's true, and that's better.
-> Thank you, Tomas.
    Old Tomas: Come back any time.
===

title: Baker
---
Elsie: Mind the flour! Oh, it's you, {player_name()}.
-> What have you got today?
    // Opening the shop ends the conversation at once.
    <<open_shop elsies_bakery>>
-> Something smells good.
    Elsie: That'll be the sweet rolls. Eight Miasma, and worth every drop.
-> Need any help?
    Elsie: Not yet, dear. Once the mill's turning, I'll need all the flour I can get.
-> Goodbye.
    Elsie: Come back hungry!
===

title: Angler
---
Wendel: Ho there, {player_name()}. Come to wet a line?
-> Show me your tackle.
    // Opening the shop ends the conversation at once.
    <<open_shop wendels_tackle>>
-> How do I fish?
    Wendel: Hold a rod in your hand, and click the water to cast.
    Wendel: With a ledger rod, watch the tip. Something nibbles first: leave it. When a fish bites, strike, quick!
    Wendel: Then hold to reel it in. When it runs, let it go, or your line snaps. When it tires, bring it home.
    -> What bites on what?
        Wendel: Worms for the river fish: dace, gudgeon, roach and chub. Paste for bream, once you've the reel for them.
        Wendel: Predators like perch take live shrimp, or chase a spinner. Every fish has its tastes.
    -> Thanks, Wendel.
        Wendel: Tight lines!
-> I've caught some fish.
    Wendel: Let's see them. I'll buy anything you pull out of the water.
    <<open_shop wendels_tackle>>
-> Goodbye.
    Wendel: Tight lines!
===
